","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"direction-neutral, expecting a large move"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a debit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Unlimited on the upside, bounded by zero on the downside"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Total premium paid, anywhere between the two strikes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Upper strike plus total premium, and lower strike minus total premium"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta neutral · gamma positive · theta negative · vega positive"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Long Strangle"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"A long out-of-the-money call and a long out-of-the-money put, same expiry. The\r\nlower-cost relative of the long straddle."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"Two long legs at different strikes, both out of the money, usually placed\r\nsymmetrically around spot. Total premium is lower than the equivalent straddle\r\nbecause neither leg has intrinsic value and both are further from the money."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"The same four exposures as a long straddle, all attenuated."}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," positive but lower at entry than a straddle's, since gamma peaks at\r\nthe money and both legs are away from it. Gamma rises as the underlying\r\napproaches either strike."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," negative but smaller in absolute terms — out-of-the-money options\r\ncarry less extrinsic value to lose per day."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," positive. Note that out-of-the-money options carry proportionally more\r\nvega relative to their price than at-the-money options do, so a strangle is\r\nmore ",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"percentage"}],"-sensitive to a volatility change than a straddle, even though\r\nits absolute vega is lower."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Payoff versus the straddle"}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"The comparison is the reason to choose between them, and it is not simply\r\n\"cheaper\"."}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"A straddle loses its maximum only at exactly one price. A strangle loses its\r\nmaximum across the entire range between the strikes — a much larger set of\r\noutcomes. In exchange, the maximum is a smaller number."}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":"A strangle's breakevens are further apart than a straddle's on the same\r\nunderlying, so it needs a larger move to profit, but it needs less money at\r\nrisk to get there. Which is preferable depends on the shape of the expected\r\nmove rather than on cost alone: a strangle suits a scenario where a very large\r\nmove is plausible, a straddle where a moderate one is."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Skew makes the strangle asymmetric."}]," The out-of-the-money put trades at\r\nhigher implied volatility than the equidistant out-of-the-money call. A\r\nsymmetric-strike strangle is therefore not a symmetric-cost position — more of\r\nthe premium is spent on the put side. Choosing strikes by equal premium rather\r\nthan equal distance produces a differently shaped position, with the call\r\nstrike closer to spot than the put."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Event pricing."}]," As with straddles, implied volatility rises into scheduled\r\nevents and collapses after. A strangle bought into an event faces the same\r\nvolatility crush, and because out-of-the-money options are proportionally more\r\nvega-sensitive, the percentage damage from the crush is worse."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Liquidity."}]," Strikes two or three steps out in NIFTY weeklies are liquid.\r\nThe equivalent strikes in a monthly-only index like BANKNIFTY, or in a single\r\nstock, may not be — and a strangle's economics are sensitive to paying the\r\nspread on two legs at entry and two at exit."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Expiry cadence."}]," NIFTY weekly on Tuesday, BANKNIFTY and the other indices\r\nmonthly on the last Tuesday, SENSEX weekly on Thursday. A monthly-only strangle\r\nholds gamma for weeks rather than days, changing the theta burden\r\nsubstantially."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":"The underlying moves, but not far enough. A strangle rewards magnitude, and a\r\nmove that would have paid a straddle handsomely can leave a strangle at a total\r\nloss because it never cleared the further strike. The second pattern is the\r\nevent trade described above."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/long-straddle.md"}]," — narrower breakevens, higher cost"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/short-strangle.md"}]," — the other side"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"volatility/smile-and-skew.md"}]," — why the two legs are not priced symmetrically"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/volatility/long-strangle.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":[["$","title",null,{"children":"404: This page could not be found."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"fontFamily":"system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,\"Apple Color Emoji\",\"Segoe UI Emoji\"","height":"100vh","textAlign":"center","display":"flex","flexDirection":"column","alignItems":"center","justifyContent":"center"},"children":["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","style",null,{"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"body{color:#000;background:#fff;margin:0}.